          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Requests the AI gateway refused before it called any provider, split by the bounded reason code. Nothing above this row can show them: no provider was dialed, so there is no upstream latency, no token count, and no cost. The reason names the fix. tools_mcp_unsupported, store_unsupported, previous_response_id_unsupported and conversation_unsupported mean a client is asking for a provider feature this gateway governs, so change the client or route it elsewhere. prompt_reference_not_found, prompt_object_unresolved, prompt_object_unrenderable and prompt_render_failed mean a stored prompt is missing or will not render, so check the prompt layer. malformed_json, body_not_object, role_missing and role_unsupported mean a client is sending bodies the shim cannot read. This family is registered on first use, so an empty panel means no request has been refused since the process started, not a broken scrape. Runbook: docs/operator-runbook.md#rb-ai-admission."
