      "description": "Fraction of the requests arriving on each AI surface that the gateway refused before dispatch. The two families share the surface label, so this is a join and not an estimate. A surface with no refusal produces no line at all rather than a zero, which is why an empty panel here is good news. Red is 5 percent, the point where SBPROXY-AI-ADMISSION-REFUSAL-SHARE files a ticket. These refusals answer 4xx, so the inbound availability SLO reads 1.0 the whole time they run and no error-rate panel moves. This is the panel that shows a client integration breaking against the gateway. When a surface climbs, read the reason breakdown to the left, then either fix the caller or enable the feature it is asking for. Runbook: docs/operator-runbook.md#rb-ai-admission."
