      "description": "Reconciles inbound AI traffic against provider traffic on one axis. Arrived counts every request classified onto an AI surface. Dispatched counts requests attributed to a provider. Refused counts requests denied before any provider was dialed. When Arrived holds steady and Dispatched drops, the missing requests should appear on Refused. If they do not, the loss is somewhere this funnel cannot see: the model allow and block gate, a virtual-key policy, a guardrail, a budget, a rate limiter, or a CEL or Rego policy each record on their own plane, and only five inbound refusal arms report here. Refused draws no line until the first refusal, because the family is registered on first use. Runbook: docs/operator-runbook.md#rb-ai-admission."
